WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.450
Zefy... Please.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.870
Lord Becknam!

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.830
I want you to survive.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.720
Lord Becknam...

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.760
If that is what you wished of me, I...

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:17.150
"Distant Ricordanza"

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.790
Oh, right, we're...

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.710
Good morning, Pacifica.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.470
Morning. Did you sleep well?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.550
No, not really.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.180
Oh.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.640
Say, Raquel...

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.890
What's this war all about, anyway?

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.570
Hey, for the time being, why don't 
you take a bath and get freshened up?

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.030
What bath?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.030
It looks like this room here has 
pretty much everything you need.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.700
They call this a bath?

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.630
W-What the heck is this?!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.520
Hey, wait a minute! What's going on?!

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.160
Quit it! Help me!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.680
What a lousy experience that was...

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.560
Still, it's awfully amazing.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.190
Yeah, it's like a dream.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:37.650
Or more like it's all 
beyond our comprehension.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.570
You awake?

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.430
Would you mind coming up here for a minute?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.950
Wow, look at the size of that crayfish!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.370
Wrong.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.760
It's a lobster.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.910
They're very delicious.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.440
So, what's the deal?

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.300
What are you trying to get 
out of us with this food?

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.170
I should warn you, we don't know anything.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.130
I never expected to get any 
information from you people.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:06.100
I just wanted to make 
sure of your intentions.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.100
Come to the capital of Leinwan.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.480
You have a grace period of fifteen days.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.100
For every day you are late, 
I will kill 1,000 people.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.690
Well, <i>I'm </i>going to Sauer for various reasons,

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.030
so I guess my asking is 
a bit of a moot point.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.950
Still... Are you sure about this?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.000
It's not as if we have a choice.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.120
It's a trap. No doubt about it.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.880
You must've known this day would come 
when you made the world your enemy.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.090
I suppose we did.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.840
In addition to Steyr, two 
additional Artillery-types

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.590
will probably be waiting 
for you at the capital.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.050
There's also a chance the people at the 
capital have been turned into proxies.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.970
You don't have a hope of 
winning, not when you had

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.020
so much trouble with just Steyr.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.480
Well, I don't intend to 
go down without a fight.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.980
Still, it's a bad idea to 
go there with this thing.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.480
The situation will escalate too far.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.990
This situation escalated 
a long, long time ago.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.450
The fate of the world hinges on this.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.890
You two might just see it as a question 
of protecting your little sister, though.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.370
Are you one to talk?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.330
Aren't <i>you </i>only doing this 
because you're out for revenge?

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.300
Heading to Sauer after dropping 
off most of your men...

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.150
That doesn't seem like a very 
rational decision to me.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.800
I won't deny that.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.260
I'm going to avenge my men.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.670
I can't think of anything else, that's why.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.480
If you like, we can still 
drop you off on land.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.050
Hey, Shannon Cassul.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:40.440
What will you do if your sister is killed?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.820
Raquel Cassul. What about you?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.440
We'll never let that happen.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.220
Good answer.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.820
But you should face facts.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.110
You're about to walk into the jaws of death

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:56.080
for the sake of a thousand total strangers.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.540
But we have to go anyway.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.100
We don't have any idea what we ought to do.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:08.240
I don't have any idea what's right anymore.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.850
But nothing will change if we don't go.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.100
If we go, things might work out for the best.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.480
So... We have to go.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.560
Might work out, huh?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.940
As a statement of intent goes, 
that's pretty wishy-washy.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.070
Well, I guess I don't have much choice.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.490
The Skid will continue 
with its raid on Sauer.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.810
Is that all right with you?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:42.710
Have you ever given any thought 
to the name of this continent?

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.560
Dustvin...

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.880
As I recall, it meant garbage 
can in the old language.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.090
I don't know who came up with the word,

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.220
but it's pretty insulting, don't you think?

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.890
Humanity's been tossed 
into this sealed-off world

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.850
like so much organic trash and locked away.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.310
What do you mean, locked away?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.480
The "demons" referred to in the 
Church of Mauser's Genesis myths

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.490
were humans like the Dark Lord Browning

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.780
and his faction who created powerful weapons.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.240
So what you're saying is,

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.740
the ones who fought the gods 
were our distant ancestors?

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.290
That's right.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:23.790
Ancient humans fought what the Church 
of Mauser calls God and lost.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.340
Humanity, having been sealed away, 
is ruled by the Church of Mauser

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.880
and is under the constant 
observation of the Peacemakers.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.720
Their reign has continued for 5,000 years.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.440
Humans back then had power 
that we can't even dream of.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.140
In other words, this Skid here

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.520
and the demons are weapons 
created by humans long ago.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.020
Along with having most of their civilization 
and knowledge stolen from them,

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:51.200
the territory humanity could live in was 
restricted to this continent of Dustvin.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.740
But with the passage of many years,

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.990
humanity even forgot that 
they'd been sealed in here.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:08:00.000
Our current civilization is modeled 
after a period called the Middle Ages

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.960
that existed about 6,000 years ago.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.130
Humanity isn't free to 
develop its own civilization

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.770
while we're under Peacemaker observation.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.970
The few remaining human forces on the outside

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.850
put together a plan to liberate humanity.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:18.970
To let humanity shatter the shell of 
this sealed-off world and be set free,

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.930
we must first defeat those Peacemakers.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.520
What they sent in here 5,000 
years ago to beat those things

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:29.660
were the genes of you three and 
the Dragoons meant to support you.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.990
Using something called human genetics,

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.990
genes that they seeded according 
to precise calculations

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.160
have now sprouted after 
more than 5,000 years.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:43.910
They produced you, the Providence 
Breaker and her Guardians.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.410
Even the Grendel Revelations

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.750
are nothing more than a 
regulatory mechanism for humans

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.630
that makes use of the religion 
called the Church of Mauser.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.920
You're able to repel the Peacemakers' 
administrator privileges...

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.810
That is, their superiority 
due to Providence...

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.570
And possess the desire to defeat them.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:05.020
And not only that, you can infect the 
people around you with that desire.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.900
Plus, the Peacemakers are unable to kill you.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.900
Because the Peacemakers haven't been 
granted the authority to do so.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.920
Pacifica Cassul.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.370
You're humanity's ace in the hole.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.560
All this must come as a shock, huh?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.290
I'm sorry...

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.250
Could you explain that 
again from the beginning?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.300
Why, you little brat!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.760
Now, now, Princess Senes.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.220
Putting it <i>very </i>simply,

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.060
the ancient people who had fought 
against the gods and lost

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.560
kept up their struggle, and as a 
result, you three and the Dragoons

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.850
are here with us now.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.690
Even if you put it that way...

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.190
It's hard to wrap your head around, isn't it?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.860
You two don't understand, either?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.520
I suppose it's only natural.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:59.360
We'll have to take a little 
more time to explain things.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.410
Director, we're 30 hexes from 
Leinwan territorial waters.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.910
Good. Change the Skid over to cruiser mode.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.430
What's that?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.340
An earthquake?

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:29.520
Changeover to cruiser mode, 48%.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.360
No abnormalities detected so far.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.580
Skid changeover to cruiser mode,

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:54.890
100% complete.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:58.550
System check... All sections green.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.010
Good.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.510
Activate Skid. Destination, 
Leinwan's capital.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:03.970
Sauer.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.810
Really, thank you for everything.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:16.650
I don't know how to thank you.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.440
Please, don't worry about it.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:21.910
It was about time for me 
to return home, anyway.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.410
A problem shared is a problem halved.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.630
So anyway, why are you headed 
to Sauer, Miss Winia?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.910
To see the person that I got a letter from.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.960
Oh, I see. That's a good idea.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.000
But I haven't told this 
person that I'm coming,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.300
so I hope it doesn't cause any trouble.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.550
Ah, how courteous you are!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.430
But, well, like they say, you 
have to take your best shot.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.490
Um, that's not to say that you should 
<i>literally</i> take a shot at anyone, understand?

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:48.010
Sure.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.980
Our waters have been breached?

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.190
Yes, sir.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:54.940
Go on.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:59.230
Reports say that after exchanging 
fire with a Giat home fleet,

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.320
the promontory which we believed 
to be Scarlet's main base

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:06.620
began to move under its own power and 
has violated our territorial waters.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.120
You're telling me that a spit of land moved?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:10.660
Yes, sir.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.080
According to wizard reports 
from the unit that I've had

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.100
tailing and observing the 
Scrapped Princess and her party,

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.570
the fleet they engaged, Giat's 
Second Fleet, was wiped out,

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:24.090
and during the fight, they observed some 
sort of enormous, tentacled creatures.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.100
What do you think of this, Luke?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.560
I believe it is most likely identical to 
what was observed in the town of Taurus.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.000
Interesting...

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:39.520
The Scrapped Princess has made contact 
with Peacemakers, as well as Scarlet...

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.270
This is certainly food for thought.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.760
Output is dropping! Speed 
has fallen below 20!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:08.970
If this keeps up, we'll be dead in the water.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.310
What is it? What happened?

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.350
I don't know.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.980
I shut down the propulsion 
systems of this mobile fortress.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.600
Why would you two...

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.940
This is unacceptable.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.360
Deliberately proceeding to a location 
you know full well to be a trap

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.190
is not a sane act.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.490
What did you say?

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.950
You should maintain the status quo

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:31.660
and wait until the Providence Breaker's 
innate abilities manifest in their true form.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.860
If we don't go there,

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.620
a thousand of the capital's 
people will be killed each day!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.060
And they'd do it, too...

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.380
If we waited for the brat's birthday...

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:45.590
A rough calculation would put the 
casualty count at over 40,000 people.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.430
Some losses are to be expected.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.050
Zefiris. Do you agree with her?

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:52.760
I do.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.730
You'll stand by and do nothing 
while people are being killed?

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.190
Nothing can be done about that.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.320
If the ship is stopped, we just 
need to get it moving again.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.440
It'll still move?

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.860
Give me a hand, Shannon Cassul.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.150
But how will you do that?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.660
Relax, I didn't ask for your help.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.440
Hey, what's with that tone of voice?

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.330
You're getting on my nerves!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.870
It's not like Natalie destroyed 
the Skid or anything.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.060
If she just severed the power linkages,

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:24.150
all we have to do is reconnect them by hand.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.760
Re... connect? What's that mean?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.880
Beats me...

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.760
Anyway, I'm sure those two

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.850
were programmed to be unable 
to harm human beings.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:38.980
That's why they did something as 
indirect as stopping the ship.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.150
I don't really get any of this,

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.530
but if we can get the ship moving 
again, let's hurry up and do it.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.030
This area up ahead is a sealed sector.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.830
For the time being, we'll 
have Eirote guiding us,

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.660
but I don't know what's going to happen.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.170
Didn't you say it would be safe?

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:04.540
There's no guarantee that we won't 
trigger the security system.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.630
If anything happens, I want 
you two to back me up.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.140
So we're basically playing it by ear, huh?

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.280
I don't understand any of this, though...

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:14.640
Just be careful you don't get in the way.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.220
What's your problem, lady?!

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.230
Stop trying to pick a fight 
with me every chance you get!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.150
Let's go. We're headed for the core area.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.230
Hey! Look at me when I'm...

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.360
Eirote!!

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:32.910
Geez...

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:41.670
Wow, so this is the sort of 
place where demons lived, huh?

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.030
Demons, huh?

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.210
I'm amazed that after all we told you,

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.550
you're still spouting nothing 
but superstitious nonsense.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.970
Hey, everything you guys know was 
taught to you by Natalie, y'know?

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.300
Don't talk so big.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.430
I see you're a master of 
the art of backtalk...

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.140
Your personality is way too 
twisted, you know that?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.390
That's <i>my </i>line.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.850
I'll put up with your chatter, but 
stop ending everything with "y'know."

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.400
Those two seem to be warming 
up to each other quite nicely.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.400
What's the problem, y'know?

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.820
Wow, this is amazing...

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:13.700
But what did humans build 
something like this <i>for</i>, anyway?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.070
They used it to fight.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:15.820
Against who?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.350
Hey, Eirote!

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.660
Put it in words small enough 
for Her Highness to understand.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:22.290
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.170
According to Natalie, ancient 
humanity came under attack

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.560
by what she called an alien intelligence.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:29.750
Alien?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:32.840
Dragoons such as Zefiris and Natalie,

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:36.430
as well as bio-weapons such as the 
Bugs, were developed one after another,

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.300
but they didn't provide 
any conclusive results.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:42.880
In the end, humanity's leader, 
a man named George Browning,

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:45.440
proposed a radical solution.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.520
Browning?

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.980
It's a person's name.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.270
He was human?!

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.230
Princess Senes, take the next right.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.820
He installed the mind of a woman named Celia,

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.610
who had the greatest precognitive 
ability of the time,

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.660
along with machinery to augment her thoughts

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.240
into a mobile fortress like this one,

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.730
creating a system that predicted the future

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:06.010
to counter the alien intelligence's attack.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
To intercept enemies which could 
appear from nowhere out of thin air,

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.670
humanity responded by 
pairing up a precognitive

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:15.050
with the power of an enormous 
artificial intelligence.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.520
The precognitive, Celia,

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:20.850
predicted enemy movements with 
a high degree of accuracy.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.890
By relying on Celia's predictions,

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.730
humanity was barely able to 
fight them on an equal footing.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.720
But that woman...

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:29.690
Celia betrayed humanity.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.150
How come?

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.330
Princess Senes, be careful.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:40.920
I'm starting to have trouble seeing you.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.750
They've entered the tampering field.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.570
I really think it would be faster

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:55.060
to hack into the field's systems 
and brainwash the Guardians.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.110
I was under the impression that

00:17:57.110 --> 00:18:00.990
we Dragoons aren't permitted to 
interfere with a human's free will.

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:04.540
I'm no longer a Dragoon.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.980
I'm a virtual personality who is borrowing 
space in the Skid's core systems.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.070
You seem unhappy.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.440
Your methods are rather forceful.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.280
You're too soft, Zefiris.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.910
Our objective is to carry 
out the plan, remember?

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.840
The plan...

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:25.500
Natalie...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.710
Is what we're trying to do really...

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.670
Have you become attached to them?

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:32.990
Very well.

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:36.080
But see to it that you don't interfere.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.370
What should I...

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:58.490
Is your research coming along well?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.450
Prince Forsyth...

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.740
It's not easy, is it?

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:05.660
All records dealing with the Scrapped 
Princess have been destroyed.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:09.710
Say, Chris. Who <i>are </i>you, really?

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:15.000
I'm a member of the Obstinate 
Arrows Special Forces unit.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.820
I see. That explains a lot.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.510
I have a favor to ask you.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.260
A favor?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:26.390
I don't know why you're 
investigating my sister,

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:29.020
but would you let me help you?

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:30.970
I'm sorry, but that's...

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:32.840
If that's out of the question,

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.020
would you at least tell 
me what you've turned up?

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:41.280
It's possible that I was 
the one who was abandoned.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.490
I have a duty to find out if that's the case.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.670
Um... Highness...

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.450
Not Highness.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:49.230
It's Forsyth.

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:57.270
Damn it, which way do we go?

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.600
Eirote! Hey!

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.260
Eirote!

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:05.370
No answer, huh?

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:09.270
Pacifica?!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.750
Shannon?! Pacifica?!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.350
Where did they...

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.730
Son of a...

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.740
Pacifica?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.660
Raquel?!

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.290
Are those two behind this?

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:29.120
Nowhere to go but forward, I guess...

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.870
Shannon Cassul.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.540
Geez, what's going on here?

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.510
Where did everybody go?!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:45.470
Pacifica Cassul.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.440
Zefiris?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.600
Look, I got separated from the others.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.480
What's the matter?

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:58.440
Pacifica Cassul, I...

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.310
What should I do?

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.200
The Skid mobile fortress 
is dead in the water.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:38.390
The three Cassul siblings 
are separated by Natalie

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:41.040
when they try to reactivate it.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.400
What in the world is Natalie up to?

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:46.460
Is she doing it because she can't 
stand how close the three of them are?

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.170
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:49.590
"Lost Quintet."

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
